  "ownsLevel": {
    "confidence": "verified",
    "items": [
      "Changing `EncSkeleton01Melee1H` 02D1DE also needs `DLC01SoulCairnKeeperBowArrow` 0074F9:Dawnguard.esm (Keeper, PC×1.2 [10–80]; on *Soul Cairn Undead*); `…Melee1Hshield` 02D1FD also needs `DLC01SoulCairnKeeperShield` 007B0F:Dawnguard.esm (Keeper) and Verrick Tilwald; `…Melee2H` 02D1E0 also needs `DLC01SoulCairnKeeper2H` 0074F8:Dawnguard.esm (Keeper, PC×1 [10–80]); `…Missile` 02D1FC also needs the advcyrus archer. Each uses the row as its template without `Stats`. The corpse `DBTreasCorpseSkeleton` 0F23B8 does the same with 02D1DE.",
      "Potema's Remains uses `dunLabyrinthianSkeletonMage` without `Stats`, and Ulfnir uses `EncDraugr01Template` the same way: each keeps its own player-scaled level when the row changes.",
      "The skeleton-race records with no template are filed elsewhere: the Reaper on *Soul Cairn Undead*; the CC necromancy skeletons on Conjured → *Undead Summons*; the unused Soul Cairn skeletons, `ccRMSSSE001_Skeleton01Summon`, `ccVSVSSE004_ChildSkeleton` and `ccBGSSSE031_Corpse` on the *Skeletons* group page.",
      "Every other skeleton record (the Volkihar `_Ambush` copies, `dunpoiSkeletonMageAggro`, `LvlSkeletonMeleeMixed`, `dunLabyrinthianSkeletonCharger` and the `TreasCorpseSkeleton*` corpses) carries `Stats` and follows its template or list."
    ]
  },
